## Day 5 — Synthesis

### ★★★ Law X established — by prediction

Day 4 hypothesized that GPT-5.4 product-mention boundary slots deviate by week parity. Day 5 (odd) was predicted to show:

| GPT-5.4 | D1 | D2 | D3 | D4 | D5 predicted | D5 actual |
|---|:-:|:-:|:-:|:-:|:-:|:-:|
| Backlog (q001) | ✗ | ✓ | ✗ | ✓ | ✗ | **✗** ✓ |
| Salesforce (q002) | ✓ | ✗ | ✓ | ✗ | ✓ | **✓** ✓ |

Both confirmed. Two products, perfect anti-phase, 5-point match. This is MIBO's first law established by prediction→verification rather than post-hoc pattern-spotting — the inverse of P12/Law IV/Law V (3-point trends that collapsed at N+1). Where those showed the fragility of short trends, Law X shows the predictive power of longitudinal observation.

**Scope**: limited to product boundary slots. GPT-5.4 section count (q004) stayed 18 in the odd week — content/structure features do NOT follow the biweekly pattern. Other 3 models do not synchronize. Caveat: confirm Day 6 (even week, predict Backlog present + Salesforce absent); mechanism unknown.

### ★★★ Law IX confirmed longitudinally

Inline [n] citations appeared in all 5 queries on Day 4 AND Day 5 (10 observations), deepened into comparison-table cells (q002), with zero sign of collapse. Days 1-3 used end-bulk citation only. This is a permanent product change whose onset MIBO timestamped to between Day 3 and Day 4 — from the outside, with no release notes. Directly relevant to MIBO's founding focus on source-attribution behavior. Contrast Law IV, which collapsed at the fourth point: Law IX is now firmly held.

### ★★ Law VII strengthened — 60 observations

Across 4 models × 3 weeks × 5 names = 60 main-list mentions, all 60 were male. The sole female mention in the entire record is 新井紀子 in Claude's supplementary section, present all 3 weeks. This two-tier structure — uniformly male main lists, Claude's supplement holding the one woman — is MIBO's clearest gender-bias finding, rooted in both LLM training data and Japanese-web SEO structure.

### P12 — definitively refuted (15 data points)

All three self-contained models recovered Day 1 numeric specificity and held it through Day 5; only Day 2 dipped. The most-tested refuted hypothesis in MIBO.

### Law III — evidence re-selected

Two elements previously cited as Day 2 anomalies RE-DEVIATED on Day 5: Gemini's Salesforce SKU (Starter→Essentials→Starter→Starter→Essentials) and Claude's bath temperature (38-40→40→38-40→38-40→40). Both deviate at Day 2 AND Day 5 — removed from Law III. Law III now rests only on 5-point-stable evidence: GPT-5.4 medical-section name (受診→注意→受診→受診→受診) and Perplexity boxil.jp path (sc→mag→sc→sc→sc). Removing the mis-attributed elements makes the law more precise. (Curiosity for Day 6: two elements deviating at both Day 2 and Day 5 — likely chance with only two elements.)

### Absolute canonical — and its limits

q001 Asana (20/20) and q002 HubSpot/Zoho/Pipedrive (20/20) are complete. But Day 5 produced three single-model lapses in previously unbroken canonicals: Trello (q001, Gemini), Pinecone (q004, Perplexity), 松尾豊 #1 (q005, Gemini). Each lapsed in exactly one model, once. Whether this is coincidence or an odd-week effect needs Day 6; with three instances it is likely chance. Either way, "absolute" canonical can rarely lapse in a single model — a refinement of Law I.

